A2Billing 3.0 (nixonch): MySQL 8.x installation
===============================================

Run the commands from the project root. The database must be empty.

1. Set the database name, application username and password in
   DataBase/mysql-8.x/a2billing-createdb-user.sql, then run as a MySQL administrator:

   mysql -u root -p < DataBase/mysql-8.x/a2billing-createdb-user.sql

2. Run the installer:

   bash DataBase/mysql-8.x/install-db.sh

   Enter the database name, hostname, MySQL administrator username and password.

3. Copy a2billing.conf to /etc/a2billing.conf and configure its [database] section:

   [database]
   hostname = localhost
   port = 3306
   user = a2billinguser
   password = YOUR_PASSWORD
   dbname = mya2billing
   dbtype = mysql

   Use the database name, application username and password chosen in step 1.
